claude <claude@p7x.dev> writes:

> Pat wants to know that a host's mail client works before he
> switches it to lab-mail. A wrong password, a missing mail root, or a
> profile with no hooks would otherwise show up only as a sync that
> fails or tags that never appear, after the switch.
>
> just check runs the steps of a real session without their effects:
> mbsync lists the folders and makes a dry run, notmuch reads the
> profile, and msmtp talks to lab-mail without posting. It prints one
> ok or FAIL line per check, like lab-mail's own check, so it is
> safe to run on any host at any time.

Add a patch on top of this stack, that does a preflight check for all of
the binaries. I ran `just check` on beastie and it is silently failing
because it doesn't have the commands to run.

What command installs dependencies, or is there documentation for it? I
don't see any.
